WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.246
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:05.546 --> 00:00:09.129
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.429 --> 00:00:15.402
Unit four: Countable & Uncountable Nouns. Today you will choose the right quantity word for each noun.

4
00:00:15.702 --> 00:00:18.401
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.367 --> 00:00:22.588
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:24.439
Countable.

7
00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:28.193
Countable means possible to count one by one.

8
00:00:28.783 --> 00:00:30.226
Apples are countable.

9
00:00:30.817 --> 00:00:33.248
Your turn. Say: Countable.

10
00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.008
Countable.

11
00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:38.937
Uncountable.

12
00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:42.878
Uncountable means not possible to count one by one.

13
00:00:43.483 --> 00:00:45.077
Water is uncountable.

14
00:00:45.683 --> 00:00:47.999
Your turn. Say: Uncountable.

15
00:00:50.833 --> 00:00:51.904
Uncountable.

16
00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:53.361
Some.

17
00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:57.627
Some means an unknown amount, used in positive sentences.

18
00:00:58.217 --> 00:00:59.763
I have some apples.

19
00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:03.026
Your turn. Say: Some.

20
00:01:05.867 --> 00:01:06.624
Some.

21
00:01:07.383 --> 00:01:08.071
Any.

22
00:01:09.083 --> 00:01:11.977
Any means an amount used in questions and negatives.

23
00:01:12.583 --> 00:01:13.933
Do you have any milk?

24
00:01:14.517 --> 00:01:16.414
Your turn. Say: Any.

25
00:01:19.267 --> 00:01:20.070
Any.

26
00:01:20.817 --> 00:01:21.655
Much.

27
00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:25.474
Much means a large amount of uncountable things.

28
00:01:26.083 --> 00:01:27.700
I don't have much time.

29
00:01:28.283 --> 00:01:30.181
Your turn. Say: Much.

30
00:01:33.033 --> 00:01:33.779
Much.

31
00:01:34.517 --> 00:01:35.367
Many.

32
00:01:36.383 --> 00:01:39.114
Many means a large number of countable things.

33
00:01:39.717 --> 00:01:41.310
There aren't many chairs.

34
00:01:41.917 --> 00:01:44.023
Your turn. Say: Many.

35
00:01:46.867 --> 00:01:47.659
Many.

36
00:01:48.417 --> 00:01:49.220
Water.

37
00:01:50.217 --> 00:01:52.367
Water means the clear liquid that we drink.

38
00:01:52.983 --> 00:01:54.368
Water is important.

39
00:01:54.983 --> 00:01:57.241
Your turn. Say: Water.

40
00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:00.904
Water.

41
00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:02.558
Apples.

42
00:02:03.550 --> 00:02:06.095
Apples means round fruits that grow on trees.

43
00:02:06.683 --> 00:02:08.265
I ate two apples.

44
00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:11.433
Your turn. Say: Apples.

45
00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:15.245
Apples.

46
00:02:16.033 --> 00:02:19.905
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:24.006
Visal, can we count apples? Can we count water?

48
00:02:25.117 --> 00:02:37.036
We can count apples: one apple, two apples. We cannot count water, so it is uncountable. Uncountable nouns have no plural and no a or an.

49
00:02:38.150 --> 00:02:40.150
Which quantity words do we use?

50
00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:51.800
With countable nouns: many, a few, some. With uncountable nouns: much, a little, some. Use any in questions and negatives.

51
00:02:52.883 --> 00:02:54.511
Are there any tricky nouns?

52
00:02:55.617 --> 00:03:07.969
Yes. Advice, information, rice and bread are uncountable. We say some advice, not an advice. To count them we use units: a piece of advice, a bowl of rice.

53
00:03:09.133 --> 00:03:11.052
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:11.917 --> 00:03:15.135
Grammar focus: Countable and uncountable nouns.

55
00:03:15.435 --> 00:03:16.610
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:17.317 --> 00:03:18.945
many apples (countable)

57
00:03:19.850 --> 00:03:21.490
much water (uncountable)

58
00:03:22.383 --> 00:03:24.476
a piece of advice (count with a unit)

59
00:03:25.433 --> 00:03:33.984
Use many with countable nouns, much with uncountable nouns and some / any with both. Uncountable nouns have no plural: advice, rice, water.

60
00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:37.727
Be careful! Don't say: I need an advice.

61
00:03:39.667 --> 00:03:42.049
Say: I need some advice.

62
00:03:42.349 --> 00:03:44.001
Advice is uncountable.

63
00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:47.534
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:48.333 --> 00:03:49.474
At the Market.

65
00:03:49.774 --> 00:03:52.865
There are many apples in the basket, but there isn't much water.

66
00:03:53.867 --> 00:03:56.902
Do you have any rice? I need some for dinner.

67
00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:00.457
How many eggs do you want, and how much milk?

68
00:04:01.467 --> 00:04:05.835
Advice and information are uncountable, so we say a piece of advice.

69
00:04:06.833 --> 00:04:10.435
Countable nouns have a plural, but uncountable nouns do not.

70
00:04:11.533 --> 00:04:15.767
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:16.617 --> 00:04:18.303
How blank apples are there?

72
00:04:18.603 --> 00:04:21.502
A, much. B, many. C, any.

73
00:04:25.067 --> 00:04:26.799
The answer is B: many.

74
00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:29.450
I don't have blank time.

75
00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:32.905
A, many. B, much. C, a few.

76
00:04:36.467 --> 00:04:38.130
The answer is B: much.

77
00:04:39.283 --> 00:04:40.993
Which noun is uncountable?

78
00:04:41.293 --> 00:04:44.354
A, apple. B, bottle. C, rice.

79
00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:49.691
The answer is C: rice.

80
00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:52.455
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:52.755 --> 00:04:58.138
A, I need an advice.. B, I need some advice.. C, I need advices..

82
00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:04.431
The answer is B: I need some advice..

83
00:05:05.583 --> 00:05:08.895
According to the reading, what do uncountable nouns not have?

84
00:05:09.195 --> 00:05:13.440
A, a plural. B, a meaning. C, a verb.

85
00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:19.104
The answer is A: a plural.

86
00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:23.533
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:24.383 --> 00:05:28.348
Is 'rice' countable or uncountable? Give an example sentence.

88
00:05:37.150 --> 00:05:38.615
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:38.915 --> 00:05:51.778
Rice is uncountable. We do not say one rice or two rices. We say some rice, a lot of rice or a bowl of rice. For example: I eat a bowl of rice every day.

90
00:05:52.078 --> 00:05:53.764
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:54.650 --> 00:05:59.415
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and countable and uncountable nouns.

92
00:05:59.715 --> 00:06:03.552
Today's value is precision. Choose your words and numbers with care.

93
00:06:03.852 --> 00:06:06.469
See you in Unit five. Goodbye!

94
00:06:06.769 --> 00:06:10.374
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

